Let the three integers be $a$, $b$, and $c$.
We can write this as a system of congruences:
\begin{align*}
a &\equiv 25 \pmod{47}, \\
b &\equiv 20 \pmod{47}, \\
c &\equiv 3 \pmod{47}.
\end{align*}
Adding these congruences together, we have
\begin{align*}
a+b+c &\equiv 25+20+3 \pmod{47} \\
&\equiv 48 \pmod{47}.
\end{align*}
Since $48$ is congruent to $1$ modulo $47$, the remainder when the sum of the three integers is divided by $47$ is $\boxed{1}$.The answer is: 1

