We can simplify the expression as follows:
$$\begin{aligned} \frac{2^{n+4} - 2(2^n)}{2(2^{n+3})} &= \frac{2^n \cdot 2^4 - 2 \cdot 2^n}{2 \cdot 2^n \cdot 2^3} \\ &= \frac{16 \cdot 2^n - 2 \cdot 2^n}{2 \cdot 8 \cdot 2^n} \\ &= \frac{14 \cdot 2^n}{16 \cdot 2^n} \\ &= \frac{14}{16} \\ &= \boxed{\frac{7}{8}}. \end{aligned}$$
