solution_steps:
Note that
\[\left| \frac{\beta - \alpha}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right| = \frac{| \beta - \alpha |}{| 1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta |}.\]Since $|\beta| = 1,$ $| \beta - \alpha |$ represents the distance between $\beta$ and $\alpha$ in the complex plane.  On the other hand, $| 1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta |$ represents the distance between 1 and $\overline{\alpha} \beta$ in the complex plane.

Let $P$ represent the point in the complex plane that corresponds to $\beta,$ and let $Q$ represent the point in the complex plane that corresponds to $\overline{\alpha} \beta.$  Since $|\beta| = 1,$ $P$ lies on the unit circle centered at the origin.  If $P$ lies on the unit circle, then $\overline{P}$ lies on the unit circle as well.  Since $| \overline{\alpha} \beta | = | \overline{\alpha} \cdot \overline{\beta} | = | \overline{\alpha} | \cdot | \overline{\beta} | = |\alpha| = 1,$ $Q$ also lies on the unit circle centered at the origin.  Furthermore, $\overline{Q}$ lies on the unit circle.

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair P, Q;

P = dir(110);
Q = dir(150);

draw(Circle((0,0),1));
draw((-1.2,0)--(1.2,0));
draw((0,-1.2)--(0,1.2));
draw((0,0)--P,Arrow(6));
draw((0,0)--Q,Arrow(6));
draw(P--Q,dashed);

dot("$1$", (1,0), S);
dot("$P$", P, NW);
dot("$Q$", Q, NW);
dot("$\overline{Q}$", conj(Q), SE);
[/asy]

We want to maximize $\frac{| \beta - \alpha |}{| 1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta |}.$  This occurs when the distance between $\beta$ and $\alpha$ is as large as possible, and the distance between 1 and $\overline{\alpha} \beta$ is as small as possible.  This happens when $\beta$ and $\alpha$ are collinear with the origin, so $\alpha$ is a nonreal multiple of $\beta.$  In other words, $\alpha = ki \beta$ for some real number $k.$

Then
\begin{align*}
\frac{| \beta - \alpha |}{| 1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta |} &= \frac{| \beta - ki \beta |}{| 1 - (-k i) \beta |} \\
&= \frac{| (1 - ki) \beta |}{| 1 + k i \beta |} \\
&= \frac{(1 - ki) |\beta|}{| 1 + ki \beta |} \\
&= \frac{1 - ki}{| 1 + ki \beta |}.
\end{align*}Since $|\beta| = 1,$
\[\frac{1 - ki}{| 1 + ki \beta |} = \frac{1 - ki}{| 1 + ki |}.\]Let $z = 1 + ki.$  Then $|z| = \sqrt{1^2 + (ki)^2} = \sqrt{1 + k^2},$ so
\[\frac{1 - ki}{| 1 + ki |} = \frac{1 - ki}{\sqrt{1 + k^2}} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{1 + k^2}} - \frac{k}{\sqrt{1 + k^2}} i.\]The magnitude of this expression is
\[\sqrt{\left( \frac{1}{\sqrt{1 + k^2}} \right)^2 + \left( \frac{k}{\sqrt{1 + k^2}} \right)^2} = \sqrt{\frac{1 + k^2}{1 + k^2}} = \boxed{1}.\]The answer is: 1
